# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform + editor litter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies + build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
coverage/
dist/
build/
*.tgz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment
#
# Never commit a real credential. `.env` files are local configuration only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local AutoLoop state (portable default namespace, see
# src/shared/autoloop-paths.mjs)
#
# These are MACHINE-LOCAL stores: telemetry, durable checkpoints, memory,
# evolution policy/candidates, Colima profile locks, review surfaces and
# scratch. They are recreated on demand and must never be versioned.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.autoloop/

# Evidence / telemetry namespaces when placed inside the checkout
# (AUTOLOOP_EVIDENCE_ROOT / AUTOLOOP_TELEMETRY_ROOT).
/evidence/
/telemetry/
/learning/

# Generated governance evidence for a run (the governance engine's default
# evidence store, overridable with AUTOLOOP_PI_GRAPH_OUTPUT). Operators who
# deliberately version their run evidence should delete this line and use
# `git add -f` for the specific records they want tracked.
/docs/pi-graph-output/

# Generated analysis / local captures
/generated/
*.analysis.json
*.probe.json
*.tmp

# Local declarations and operator state
production-declaration.json
*-deployment.json
review-job.json
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test-suite litter
#
# Test suites must write to the OS temp directory; these entries exist only so
# an accidental cwd-relative write can never be committed. Treat a hit as a bug
# in the suite, not as something to commit.
#
# `file:` is a real observed shape: a test that passes a `file://...` string to
# a path-taking function with the scheme intact creates a literal `file:`
# directory. It must be ignored as a FILE as well as a directory, which is why
# the rule is `file:*` and not `/file:`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
file:*
/learning-incidents*/
/transfer-metrics-core*/
/r2-cross-process*/
